  "claim_boundary": [
    "V and S share a source 500-m geometry-eligible animal population per panel; I has a distinct x-y-time/dyad/scope eligibility rule and different sample sizes in three of four panels.",
    "Matching source panel and study year is NOT proof that the V/S eligible animal identity set equals, or is a subset of, the co-use I eligible set.",
    "Matching n in P2023 (6 vs 6) is NOT proof of matching exact animal IDs; original numerical summary does not supply the cross-estimand individual intersection.",
    "Neither the count discrepancy nor source p-values supports a within-animal association between high V_rel and I, same-animal spatial response, temporal causal effect, avoidance or absence thereof.",
    "Co-use I measures session-median-centered residual-height deviations, not actual physical altitude gap; S and V use smoothed estimated distributions and are algebraically coupled.",
    "The original underlying GPS and tag-level identifiers were not reopened; do not assert the actual size of intersection of V/S and I sample IDs.",
    "A third post-outcome 500-m place×speed×turning matching test also uses a distinct set of biologically eligible animals (19/23/11/9), not the 500-m 3D V/S eligible set (8/5/6/9).",
    "The full eligible animal identity overlap across fine500, V/S and I is unverified; equal n in P2016 fine/V-S (9/9) does not establish identical bats."
